Command:        Post
Purpose:        Add a new message item to a subboard
Available at:   Message and Upload area subboard prompts, except where
                disabled.

With the proper access, Post will allow you to enter a new item into a subboard.  Other users may then respond to your item by either using the Respond command after reading your item, or by entering a new item, possibly depending on how the subboard has been configured.

The TITLE that you supply for your item must be unique to that subboard.

If enabled, you will have the option to make your item Anonymous.  That is, your name will not be displayed when other users read your item.  HOWEVER, you should be aware that system operators may be able to trace anonymous messages.

If enabled, you will have the option to make your item Private.  Only you and the person your have addressed your item to will be able to Read your private item.  All responses to a private item are automatically private.

Use HELP EDITOR for help with CNet's text editor.
